WEBVTT

00:06.156 --> 00:09.091
Jake, you're hardly touching
your salad.

00:09.092 --> 00:13.402
I promised Berta I'd cut down
on the roughage.

00:17.968 --> 00:22.304
Well, all right, ahem,
why don't I get the soup?

00:22.305 --> 00:26.008
Based on the salad,
I'm not so optimistic.

00:26.009 --> 00:29.078
So you have absolutely no idea
why she invited us here?

00:29.079 --> 00:33.048
- All she said on the phone was dinner.
- You believed her?

00:33.049 --> 00:36.452
Good God, man,
do you realize what you've done?

00:36.453 --> 00:38.821
- Just relax.
- Just relax?

00:38.822 --> 00:42.992
We'll be lucky to leave here
with all of our limbs and gonads.

00:42.993 --> 00:45.663
- What's a gonad?
- You are.

00:47.431 --> 00:49.931
So it's bad.

00:50.066 --> 00:54.246
- You're not a gonad.
- Says the other gonad.

00:55.539 --> 00:57.573
Here we go.

00:57.574 --> 00:59.008
Potato leek soup.

00:59.009 --> 01:01.509
Oh, delightful.

01:02.846 --> 01:04.513
You got any crackers?

01:04.514 --> 01:05.748
Crackers?

01:05.749 --> 01:07.950
I like having something crunchy
in my soup.

01:07.951 --> 01:11.153
Little goldfish, crouton, a stale bagel.

01:11.154 --> 01:13.756
I'll check. Go ahead and start.

01:13.757 --> 01:17.037
Captain Crunch will work in a pinch.

01:17.060 --> 01:19.428
I got a bad feeling about this, Alan.

01:19.429 --> 01:24.733
- What? We're having dinner with our mother.
- So you feel it too.

01:24.734 --> 01:28.370
What kind of person
doesn't serve crackers with soup?

01:28.371 --> 01:33.451
The only thing I have that's crunchy
is macadamia nuts.

01:33.977 --> 01:37.097
Interesting. Let's give her a try.

01:37.881 --> 01:41.984
Well, I suppose you boys
are wondering why I asked you here.

01:41.985 --> 01:45.120
You mean, this isn't just a nice,
warm family dinner?

01:45.121 --> 01:47.621
Knock it off, Charlie.

01:48.091 --> 01:49.525
I have some good news.

01:49.526 --> 01:52.026
And no, I'm not dying.

01:52.128 --> 01:56.832
I didn't say anything.
Why would you even go there?

01:56.833 --> 01:59.168
Okay, I'm sorry.

01:59.169 --> 02:02.671
Anyway, I have been doing
some financial planning.

02:02.672 --> 02:05.074
So you're thinking about dying.

02:05.075 --> 02:08.677
Trust me, darling, I promise
to stick around long enough...

02:08.678 --> 02:14.008
...to identify your bloated, gin-soaked,
syphilitic remains.

02:17.220 --> 02:19.940
Okay, so we got a time frame.

02:20.924 --> 02:23.425
So, what about your financial plan?

02:23.426 --> 02:27.796
Yes, well, ahem, one thing I've done
is to set aside enough money...

02:27.797 --> 02:33.147
...to ensure that my grandson
will get a college education.

02:44.381 --> 02:46.916
Oh, Mom, Mom, that is, uh,
that is very generous...

02:46.917 --> 02:50.019
...but, uh, I started a college fund
for Jake when he was born.

02:50.020 --> 02:52.520
Really?

02:52.822 --> 02:55.391
How much do you have in there now?

02:55.392 --> 02:57.892
Uh.

02:58.361 --> 03:02.431
Did you hear?
Grandma's sending you to college.

03:02.432 --> 03:05.392
Now? I haven't finished my soup.

03:07.137 --> 03:11.557
Mom, have you thought this through?
Look at him.

03:12.042 --> 03:16.092
Maybe there should be one child
left behind.

03:17.614 --> 03:19.748
Charlie, Charlie, just shush.

03:19.749 --> 03:22.851
Mo-- Mom, I cannot tell you
how much I appreciate this.

03:22.852 --> 03:26.388
Jake, do you understand
what your grandma is providing here?

03:26.389 --> 03:29.017
Yeah, more school. Big whoop.

03:29.192 --> 03:31.860
Well, Jake, dear,
perhaps this will help enthuse you.

03:31.861 --> 03:34.330
If, If you buckle down
and your grades improve...

03:34.331 --> 03:36.765
...when the time comes for you
to go to college...

03:36.766 --> 03:39.268
...Grandmommy
is going to buy you a new car.

03:39.269 --> 03:41.769
I love you, Grandmommy.

04:13.803 --> 04:15.504
When I get my car from Grandma...

04:15.505 --> 04:20.209
...one of you guys
is gonna have to park on the street.

04:20.210 --> 04:21.844
The car is for college.

04:21.845 --> 04:24.380
And what makes you think
you'll still be here?

04:24.381 --> 04:27.551
Oh, come on, you know you love me.

04:27.717 --> 04:29.284
He's got you. You do love him.

04:29.285 --> 04:33.775
Yeah, but he doesn't have
to rub my nose in it.

04:34.691 --> 04:36.892
So, what do you think Mom's angle is?

04:36.893 --> 04:39.328
Does she have to have an angle?

04:39.329 --> 04:42.079
A college trust fund? For him?

04:42.432 --> 04:45.868
Last week, he bit his hand
eating a sandwich.

04:45.869 --> 04:49.069
He smelled the ham, he got excited.

04:49.806 --> 04:51.573
Maybe she's just trying to buy his love.

04:51.574 --> 04:52.775
[SlGHS]

04:52.776 --> 04:57.780
Alan, think it through. She could've done
that with a pork chop and a Creamsicle.

04:57.781 --> 05:01.583
Whatever, it is a big load off my mind
knowing his education is taken care of.

05:01.584 --> 05:05.821
Oh, yeah, that's what Mom wants,
to take a load off your mind.

05:05.822 --> 05:08.490
Okay, why do you think she did it?

05:08.491 --> 05:11.293
I don't know.
But if you wanna get inside her head...

05:11.294 --> 05:16.131
...you've gotta start thinking
more twisted, manipulative, devious.

05:16.132 --> 05:17.566
For example...

05:17.567 --> 05:20.169
...if by some miracle,
he gets through college...

05:20.170 --> 05:24.339
- ...and she sends him to law school--
- Law school? You've already lost me.

05:24.340 --> 05:28.110
Maybe she's boinking Dean of Admissions.
We don't know. Just hear me out.

05:28.111 --> 05:29.511
Go on.

05:29.512 --> 05:31.580
Let's say he crawls through law school...

05:31.581 --> 05:35.718
...takes seven or eight shots at the bar.
We know how that ends.

05:35.719 --> 05:39.021
So, what are his options
as a failed lawyer?

05:39.022 --> 05:41.023
I don't know. Government work?

05:41.024 --> 05:44.193
Exactly. Maybe he lands
on the zoning commission.

05:44.194 --> 05:50.544
And bingo-bango, Mom finally gets
to put a second story on her house.

05:52.469 --> 05:56.205
You really think she's gonna send him
to college and law school...

05:56.206 --> 05:58.574
...just so she can add an extra bedroom?

05:58.575 --> 05:59.775
That's insane.

05:59.776 --> 06:02.276
Is it, Alan?

06:03.713 --> 06:06.213
Is it really?

06:15.024 --> 06:16.458
Morning.

06:16.459 --> 06:18.959
Morning.

06:21.097 --> 06:23.597
- Alan?
- Yeah?

06:24.167 --> 06:26.667
You having a stroke?

06:28.304 --> 06:30.773
No. No, I'm just--
I'm just trying to figure out...

06:30.774 --> 06:33.375
...why I need to go to work today.

06:33.376 --> 06:37.846
I mean, Mom's taking care
of Jake's education, buying him a car.

06:37.847 --> 06:40.182
Why should I bust my hump?

06:40.183 --> 06:42.217
For your self-respect?

06:42.218 --> 06:45.418
No. Judith got that in the divorce.

06:45.822 --> 06:48.090
Because you like
to heal people's back pain...

06:48.091 --> 06:49.591
...with your chiropractic magic?

06:49.592 --> 06:52.092
[SNORTS]

06:53.363 --> 06:55.631
Okay, well, you gotta go somewhere.

06:55.632 --> 06:57.666
Why?

06:57.667 --> 07:00.497
Because you're creeping me out.

07:03.606 --> 07:07.076
I should take up motivational speaking.

07:08.111 --> 07:11.079
- Morning.
- Something's wrong with your brother.

07:11.080 --> 07:14.983
We don't say the word "wrong,"
we say "special."

07:14.984 --> 07:17.853
No, it's true. My friends don't think
you're my grandma...

07:17.854 --> 07:21.054
...they think you're my young aunt.

07:23.560 --> 07:25.828
If he gets his nose further up
her keister...

07:25.829 --> 07:30.189
...we're gonna have to tie a rope
to his feet.

07:30.900 --> 07:34.670
Hey, I was thinking, you know what
would be a nice, safe vehicle for me?

07:34.671 --> 07:37.171
A used police car.

07:38.875 --> 07:42.377
I don't know. I guess from the police.

07:42.378 --> 07:44.680
She's buying lunkhead a car?

07:44.681 --> 07:46.481
And a college education.

07:46.482 --> 07:49.651
Ha, that makes sense
if it's a clown college...

07:49.652 --> 07:52.152
...and the car seats 20.

07:53.489 --> 07:56.425
All right, then I'll see you in an hour.

07:56.426 --> 07:59.276
Hold on. No, I don't need one.

08:00.730 --> 08:03.230
Okay, okay. Bye.

08:03.233 --> 08:07.302
I'm gonna spend the afternoon with
Grandma. If she asks, I took a shower.

08:07.303 --> 08:09.338
Figured out her angle yet?

08:09.339 --> 08:10.539
No.

08:10.540 --> 08:13.040
And that's what scares me.

08:13.042 --> 08:15.567
BERTA:
Bom-bom-bom.

08:17.013 --> 08:19.513
Seemed appropriate.

08:22.185 --> 08:25.654
All right, Mr. Sharipa,
how's it feel right here?

08:25.655 --> 08:27.623
SHARlPA:
A little tender.

08:27.624 --> 08:30.492
Yeah, yeah,
you've got a spasm right there.

08:30.493 --> 08:31.860
It's my own fault.

08:31.861 --> 08:36.398
I was trying to do it in the shower
with Mrs. Sharipa last night.

08:36.399 --> 08:39.163
The woman is no ballerina.

08:40.770 --> 08:43.772
Well, sex in the shower
is really a young man's game.

08:43.773 --> 08:47.473
Or a middle-aged man with a skinny wife.

08:47.744 --> 08:50.112
- Sure.
- What can I say?

08:50.113 --> 08:53.283
I like a little junk in the trunk.

08:53.483 --> 08:55.784
I-- I think that says it.

08:55.785 --> 08:57.719
Slap her on the ass at Christmas...

08:57.720 --> 09:02.110
...it doesn't stop shaking
till New Year's Eve.

09:03.559 --> 09:05.227
Just between you and me...

09:05.228 --> 09:09.518
...uh, she enjoys a little spanking
from Santa.

09:10.333 --> 09:12.000
Who doesn't?

09:12.001 --> 09:14.136
I checked the list twice...

09:14.137 --> 09:16.637
...always naughty.

09:19.842 --> 09:22.544
Uh-huh. Could you, uh,
turn on your right, Mr. Sharipa?

09:22.545 --> 09:25.948
I'll, uh, try to relieve the
pressure on your sciatic nerve.

09:25.949 --> 09:28.183
Could you cross your arms, please?
Thank you.

09:28.184 --> 09:29.584
Okay.

09:29.585 --> 09:32.085
[FARTS]

09:35.792 --> 09:38.292
Excuse me.

09:38.628 --> 09:44.158
Oh, no, that-- That happens.
It's, uh, it's perfectly natu--

09:45.101 --> 09:47.601
Oh, dear Lord.

09:48.838 --> 09:51.740
Yeah, that's the garlic clams
I had for lunch.

09:51.741 --> 09:54.751
I like them, they don't like me.

09:56.112 --> 09:57.446
Um.

09:57.447 --> 10:00.983
If you'll just excuse me for a moment.

10:00.984 --> 10:03.518
Hey, you know, I feel better.

10:03.519 --> 10:07.409
Maybe that's where the pressure
came from.

10:08.024 --> 10:10.959
- Where are you going, Dr. Harper?
- Home.

10:10.960 --> 10:13.061
Will you be coming back?

10:13.062 --> 10:15.562
Dr. Harper?

10:19.702 --> 10:22.202
Oh, my God.

10:28.911 --> 10:32.681
Check it out. This SUV comes with
a mini-fridge in the glove compartment.

10:32.682 --> 10:35.182
Fascinating.

10:35.752 --> 10:39.121
Let's spend a little time
talking about our college plans.

10:39.122 --> 10:43.358
Our plans? Are you going too?
Because that changes everything.

10:43.359 --> 10:45.293
I've already been to college, darling.

10:45.294 --> 10:48.130
They were some of the happiest years
of my life.

10:48.131 --> 10:50.098
- Really?
- Mm-hm.

10:50.099 --> 10:52.899
What kind of car did you have?

10:52.902 --> 10:56.204
Look, Jake, I understand that
you're excited about getting a car...

10:56.205 --> 10:57.806
...but keep in mind...

10:57.807 --> 11:01.209
...the car is predicated
on you getting into college.

11:01.210 --> 11:03.111
Right.

11:03.112 --> 11:05.313
What's predicated mean?

11:05.314 --> 11:07.814
No college, no car.

11:08.251 --> 11:10.318
Oh.

11:10.319 --> 11:13.088
What if I flunk out?
Do I have to give the car back?

11:13.089 --> 11:15.857
Oh, sweetheart,
what makes you think you'd flunk out?

11:15.858 --> 11:17.459
Well, history.

11:17.460 --> 11:22.330
Now there's a 60-60 chance I'm gonna
have to repeat the eighth grade.

11:22.331 --> 11:24.299
Sixty-sixty, huh?

11:24.300 --> 11:26.962
At least. It could be 70-40.

11:27.937 --> 11:30.205
Well, we can rule out the lvy League.

11:30.206 --> 11:33.646
- ls that good?
- For the lvy League.

11:34.143 --> 11:38.280
You know, dear, maybe we're
going about this the wrong way.

11:38.281 --> 11:41.183
College should be about
pursuing the things you love.

11:41.184 --> 11:42.651
Well, what do you love?

11:42.652 --> 11:45.985
Um, TV, video games, sleeping.

11:46.155 --> 11:49.991
I love sleeping so much
sometimes I actually dream about it.

11:49.992 --> 11:52.794
Okay, maybe I wasn't clear enough.

11:52.795 --> 11:54.463
Oh, you know what I really love?

11:54.464 --> 11:58.066
Twice-dipped French toast
with a sprinkling of orange zest.

11:58.067 --> 12:00.902
- Orange zest?
- You scrape it from an orange peel.

12:00.903 --> 12:02.838
It's what really makes my recipe work.

12:02.839 --> 12:04.339
You have a recipe?

12:04.340 --> 12:06.641
Yep. It kind of happened by accident.

12:06.642 --> 12:09.845
I was making once-dipped
French toast, but I dropped it.

12:09.846 --> 12:13.915
Lot of great discoveries are accidents,
like Thomas Edison and the telephone.

12:13.916 --> 12:16.416
That wasn't Thomas.

12:17.120 --> 12:20.388
- So you like to cook?
- Yeah, I love it.

12:20.389 --> 12:24.559
Because, you know, I love to eat
and I love to surprise my mouth.

12:24.560 --> 12:26.361
Well, you know, dear...

12:26.362 --> 12:29.831
...what you are talking about
is becoming a chef...

12:29.832 --> 12:31.666
...and there are schools for that...

12:31.667 --> 12:34.669
...and the potential
to make a terrific living.

12:34.670 --> 12:36.905
Do I get to wear
one of those poofy hats?

12:36.906 --> 12:38.206
If you want to.

12:38.207 --> 12:41.427
Cool. Then I guess I'll be a chef.

12:41.878 --> 12:44.312
My grandson the chef.

12:44.313 --> 12:46.448
I can live with that.

12:46.449 --> 12:52.879
Know what I could drive if I was a chef?
The Oscar Meyer Weinermobile.

13:03.900 --> 13:06.400
- Hey.
- Hey.

13:06.836 --> 13:08.870
I got a kayak.

13:08.871 --> 13:11.273
I see.

13:11.274 --> 13:12.974
Guess what I'm gonna do?

13:12.975 --> 13:15.110
Go kayaking?

13:15.111 --> 13:19.051
Yep. I have decided that life is too short.

13:19.081 --> 13:22.117
So you're going out in
the Pacific Ocean in a plastic boat.

13:22.118 --> 13:24.152
Good thinking.

13:24.153 --> 13:27.789
No, I was at work today and it suddenly
became clear to me that--

13:27.790 --> 13:28.990
[THUDS]

13:28.991 --> 13:31.491
Oh, sorry about that.

13:31.527 --> 13:34.396
It became clear to me
that I don't like what I'm doing.

13:34.397 --> 13:35.964
Mom's taking care of Jake...

13:35.965 --> 13:38.833
...I can spend my time doing things
that give me joy.

13:38.834 --> 13:42.204
So you're gonna masturbate in a kayak?

13:42.205 --> 13:44.705
No, but that's the point.

13:45.007 --> 13:47.507
You'll have to elaborate.

13:47.643 --> 13:50.143
I could, if I wanted to.

13:55.418 --> 13:58.858
Yeah, who could have seen that coming?

13:59.855 --> 14:02.355
Look, I'm sorry.

14:06.896 --> 14:11.099
Here you go. Grilled cheese
with Gouda, Swiss and monster.

14:11.100 --> 14:12.601
You mean "Muenster."

14:12.602 --> 14:14.269
No, that's an old TV show.

14:14.270 --> 14:18.139
And they're called that because
they're monsters. This is a cheese.

14:18.140 --> 14:20.442
Anyway, this sandwich
has heirloom tomatoes...

14:20.443 --> 14:23.144
...smoked applewood bacon
on sourdough toast.

14:23.145 --> 14:24.579
Where did you learn this?

14:24.580 --> 14:28.016
Food Channel, foodchannel.com,
Food Channel on Demand...

14:28.017 --> 14:32.707
...Food Channel Magazine.
And the school lunch lady.

14:32.722 --> 14:35.624
Oh, and save room
for homemade potato chips.

14:35.625 --> 14:37.892
You're making potato chips?

14:37.893 --> 14:39.094
Oh, yeah, it's easy.

14:39.095 --> 14:42.330
Slice the potatoes real thin,
rub the slices with lemon and garlic.

14:42.331 --> 14:46.001
Fry them up in a hot iron skillet
and then salt to taste.

14:46.002 --> 14:47.502
I can't get over this.

14:47.503 --> 14:49.471
- Bon appetite.
- Mm.

14:49.472 --> 14:52.722
- Teet.
- No, that's a cow's boob.

14:55.144 --> 14:57.312
Oh, my goodness.

14:57.313 --> 14:58.747
This is delicious.

14:58.748 --> 15:03.551
Don't eat more than three
or you won't poop for a week.

15:03.552 --> 15:06.021
Trust me.

15:06.022 --> 15:10.792
Well, at least we have finally found
a career path for you.

15:10.793 --> 15:15.893
Cool. I'll go get the chips
and we'll talk about cars.

15:15.931 --> 15:20.481
You know what?
Let's settle this car thing first.

15:26.375 --> 15:28.875
Oh, God, it was incredible.

15:28.944 --> 15:32.436
The-- The wind, the sky, the surf.

15:32.615 --> 15:35.175
Ah, I feel like I'm reborn.

15:39.188 --> 15:41.990
You were out there for 15 minutes.

15:41.991 --> 15:44.741
Yeah, well, my arms got tired.

15:45.695 --> 15:48.763
Oh, so you did decide to go kayanking.

15:48.764 --> 15:51.562
- What?
- Masturyaking.

15:52.168 --> 15:54.135
You're terrible.

15:54.136 --> 15:57.096
And anyway, no one could see me.

16:00.509 --> 16:02.977
- So now what?
- Now?

16:02.978 --> 16:05.811
Now I just live. I enjoy.

16:05.981 --> 16:07.716
All right.

16:07.717 --> 16:10.185
This rat has quit the race.

16:10.186 --> 16:11.453
Good for you.

16:11.454 --> 16:13.988
This hamster is off the treadmill.

16:13.989 --> 16:15.190
Glad to hear it.

16:15.191 --> 16:19.561
This squirrel is satisfied
with the nuts he has.

16:19.562 --> 16:22.062
No comment.

16:22.732 --> 16:25.232
[SlGHS]

16:26.502 --> 16:29.003
I'm not gonna make it, Charlie.

16:29.004 --> 16:30.872
Didn't think you would.

16:30.873 --> 16:32.407
No goals...

16:32.408 --> 16:34.209
...no challenges...

16:34.210 --> 16:36.544
...no gut-wrenching fear
driving me forward.

16:36.545 --> 16:38.847
I mean, how can you stand it?

16:38.848 --> 16:40.615
Me?

16:40.616 --> 16:45.253
Well, I have kind of an existential
philosophy that shapes my outlook.

16:45.254 --> 16:49.557
It involves a willingness to let life
carry me along in its wake...

16:49.558 --> 16:53.268
...as I contemplate
its infinite mystery.

16:53.929 --> 16:57.165
Plus, I drink and take a lot of naps.

16:57.166 --> 17:02.036
Yeah, well, I need something
meaningful to strive for.

17:02.037 --> 17:04.537
Sorry, I don't follow.

17:04.740 --> 17:08.943
I need a carrot in front of me
and a stick behind me. Without that l--

17:08.944 --> 17:11.444
I have no reason to live.

17:12.982 --> 17:15.482
- That's it.
- What's it?

17:16.352 --> 17:18.653
No reason to live.

17:18.654 --> 17:20.288
That's Mom's angle.

17:20.289 --> 17:26.449
It's never had anything to do with Jake.
She's trying to kill you.

17:26.662 --> 17:28.096
Oh, come on.

17:28.097 --> 17:30.098
Think about it.

17:30.099 --> 17:32.534
She takes the pressure
off your shoulders...

17:32.535 --> 17:35.136
...knowing you can't live without it.

17:35.137 --> 17:37.205
Oh, she's good.

17:37.206 --> 17:39.207
Why would Mom wanna kill me?

17:39.208 --> 17:41.843
I don't know. Why do I wanna kill you?

17:41.844 --> 17:43.778
Why does your ex-wife wanna kill you?

17:43.779 --> 17:46.899
You just bring that out in people.

17:47.049 --> 17:48.716
You're being ridiculous.

17:48.717 --> 17:52.020
Okay, okay,
let's look at the alternate explanation.

17:52.021 --> 17:55.557
For the first time in her life,
our mother is being totally selfless...

17:55.558 --> 17:59.928
...and thinking
about someone else's well-being.

18:00.095 --> 18:03.698
Dear God,
my own mother is trying to kill me.

18:03.699 --> 18:06.419
I'm glad we got that settled.

18:06.435 --> 18:08.935
It was really bugging me.

18:11.440 --> 18:14.170
[lNDlSTlNCT CHATTER OVER RADlO]

18:16.045 --> 18:19.175
- Terrific sandwich.
FlREMAN: Yeah.

18:19.949 --> 18:24.452
You'll find the fire gave everything
a nice smoky flavor.

18:24.453 --> 18:29.693
Just out of curiosity,
what does a used firetruck go for?

18:32.928 --> 18:36.097
Hey, Alan.
I got an idea that might cheer you up.

18:36.098 --> 18:38.132
I'm listening.

18:38.133 --> 18:41.169
You need a carrot and a stick
to make your life meaningful?

18:41.170 --> 18:42.737
How about this?

18:42.738 --> 18:45.540
Every month I let you give me
a small amount of money...

18:45.541 --> 18:50.445
...in exchange for the pleasure
of living in my house.

18:50.446 --> 18:53.381
We'll call it rent.

18:54.483 --> 18:57.452
Wow, it's been a long time
since I paid rent.

18:57.453 --> 19:00.493
Five years, two months, 11 days.

19:00.556 --> 19:04.125
Interesting. It would certainly give me
a reason to go back to work.

19:04.126 --> 19:06.651
Right, that's the carrot.

19:06.829 --> 19:11.065
And if you fall behind,
I get to hit you with a stick.

19:11.066 --> 19:15.203
- Very funny.
- No, I'm serious. That's my carrot.

19:15.204 --> 19:18.039
Okay, how much did you have in mind?

19:18.040 --> 19:21.999
Well, I've given it some thought...

19:23.045 --> 19:27.935
...and I think you'll find this
to be a fair number.

19:30.052 --> 19:32.086
Oh.

19:32.087 --> 19:33.855
Oh, well, uh...

19:33.856 --> 19:37.158
...if I'm paying rent, I'll get a say
in what goes on around here.

19:37.159 --> 19:39.659
No, no, no.

19:42.698 --> 19:45.198
If you want a say...

19:45.367 --> 19:47.867
...this is the number.

19:50.472 --> 19:52.574
I don't need a say.

19:52.575 --> 19:56.705
- Good. So every month on the first?
- Deal.

19:59.214 --> 20:01.716
All right. All right.
I feel good about this.

20:01.717 --> 20:04.752
Pitching in, pulling my own weight.
It's long overdue.

20:04.753 --> 20:07.221
Five years, two months, 11 days.

20:07.222 --> 20:08.489
Right.

20:08.490 --> 20:11.125
Uh, of course, since, uh,
the month has already started...

20:11.126 --> 20:13.661
- ...we'll start next month.
- Fine.

20:13.662 --> 20:17.198
Although, uh, with the holidays coming,
maybe it'd be better to start fresh...

20:17.199 --> 20:19.367
...with the new year. One, one.

20:19.368 --> 20:21.868
Sure, whatever.

20:22.204 --> 20:26.507
- Unless the economy's still in the tank.
- Always a possibility.

20:26.508 --> 20:30.111
In which case, we'll, uh, probably
wanna revisit the number.

20:30.112 --> 20:31.713
CHARLlE:
Probably.

20:31.714 --> 20:35.817
I mean, you know, the market is,
is pretty volatile right now.

20:35.818 --> 20:38.853
Uh, I think some belt-tightening is in order
for everybody.

20:38.854 --> 20:40.989
You know, landlords and tenants alike.

20:40.990 --> 20:43.490
[THUD THEN ALAN SHOUTS]

21:11.720 --> 21:14.220
[ENGLlSH SDH]
